under Coyote's own terms; the obligation MPL-2.0 section 3.2 attaches is that
recipients of a binary be told how to obtain the source of the covered files,
which are published unmodified at
https://github.com/serialport/serialport-rs. The same obligation already
applies to `colored`, a direct dependency under the same license, published
at https://github.com/mackwic/colored. The MPL-2.0 text itself is at
https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/.

This section records the obligations these dependencies add, not the full
dependency graph. Coyote's wider tree carries notice obligations that predate
these dependencies, most of them enumerated nowhere; closing that gap is a
separate piece of work.

